upstream body. sha256 below covers the PRISTINE body (strip the banner:
first 8 lines). All files MUST come from the same tag -- utils/readable/
writable/destroy share the kState bitfield layout; mixed-tag vendoring
silently corrupts it (docs/design/streams-port.md section 2).

Deliberately not vendored: lazy_transform.js (crypto extends Transform
directly), stream/consumers.js (oam keeps its own), stream/web.js +
internal/webstreams/adapters (bridged to js/streams.js; stub in slice 2).

Re-vendor procedure (Node version bump):
  1. Update TAG + COMMIT here (deref the annotated tag via the GitHub API).
  2. For each file below: fetch source-base/<path>, verify sha256 of the
     fetched body changes ONLY when upstream changed, re-prepend the banner
     (update tag/commit/date), write.
  3. Re-derive the primordials union + shim surface (slice-2 extraction
     script) BEFORE running the suite -- new upstream code may widen it.
  4. cargo run -p xtask -- node-suite && conformance; full ci-local before
     commit. All files move together or not at all.

